            <h2>12. Summary of Key Points</h2>
            <div class="section-body hover-highlight">
                <p>
                    Unit testing builds confidence in small pieces of code by verifying behavior.
                    Use AAA to structure tests and clear assertions to describe expectations.
                    Mocks and fakes isolate dependencies, keeping tests fast and deterministic.
                    Coverage and boundary tests highlight missing scenarios.
                    Consistent naming and isolation reduce flaky tests in CI pipelines.
                </p>
